WEBVTT

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.660
Sasshi and Arumi are a boy and a girl, born and raised in a very ordinary Osaka...

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.590
...in the very ordinary Abenobashi.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.120
Currently, they have been flung to an Abenobashi in another world...

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.730
...and have found themselves with no way of getting back.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.590
On top of that, wherever they go, they end up having to defeat a goblin.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.710
The reason being, they'll get to go back to their very ordinary world...

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.940
...if they use the goblin's magical powers, but...

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.650
Well, when it comes right down to it...

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.210
...these are goblins who lose to very ordinary grade school kids.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.510
So, their magical powers aren't very reliable either.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.580
And ultimately, they end up jumping to another strange world...

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.520
Huh, so it's a dinosaur kingdom this time?

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.430
It's wrong.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.300
What's wrong?! That and that and that are all dinosaurs!

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.300
It's wrong.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.700
It ain't wrong!

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.480
We keep getting sent to worlds that seem like places you'd like.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.940
It's getting on my nerves!

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.740
It's funny.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.380
It ain't funny!

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.900
Knock it off already, or I'm gonna smack you!

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.150
Don't say that after you've smacked me.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.480
It's your fault.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:08.450
That's not it. The dinosaurs here are funny.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.660
What?

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:11.950
Look, there's a Stegosaurus from the Jurassic Period together...

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.120
...with a Tyrannosaurus from the Cretaceous Period.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.710
It's just not right, see?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.360
Don't look at me.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.920
No normal grade school kid would know details like that.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.720
Oh, I know what that is!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.560
Let's see, it's a Brontosaurus!

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.690
You're wrong there though.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.770
Whoa, wait, wait!

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.210
It's true, there was a time when it was called a Brontosaurus!

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.110
You're right, you're right! Don't smack me! Don't smack me!

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.780
I am right!

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:42.530
It's true, there was a time when it was called the Brontosaurus...

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.790
...but back then, the fossils of a couple Sauropods had been mixed up...

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.560
...while reconstructing it and after a thorough investigation...

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.530
...they renamed it an Apatosaurus.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.030
Approximately 20 meters in length...

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.090
...living in the Americas towards the end of the Jurassic Period.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.130
Wow, you know a lot.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.370
If it's about creatures from the Jurassic to the Crustaceous Period, ask me anything!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.060
Hey, Professor Sasshi!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.370
I couldn't be a professor at this age.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.700
Call me "doctor"!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.980
Well, this is where you're awfully knowledgeable...

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.990
...about the specific topics that you like, but you're totally no good at schoolwork...

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.590
...and you've got dinosaur models and figurines of girls...

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:22.190
...all lined up around your room.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.110
Gradually, you'll turn into an obnoxious geek, who leads a gloomy, brooding life.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.930
Oh, how disgusting.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:28.910
Hey, what's this?

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.110
Okay, there, there. Good boy, good boy.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.970
So no one ever takes me seriously no matter what I say.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.640
Hey, what's this guy?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.300
Fine then! I'm a geek after all, right?!

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.050
What is this?!

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.770
But, but, this girl sure is cute.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.260
Arumi-chan here's asking ya what the heck this is, ya know?!

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.790
A triceratops baby, I think?

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.760
I guess that makes it Tricera-Spot.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:57.960
Here, here.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.450
Tri-Spot, Tri-Spot, hit the spot.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:01.470
Here.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:36.980
Oh, how bold of you.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.500
No!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.910
That'll do it.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.200
Get dressed!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.210
What a thing to have ended up showing you...

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.250
What's it matter? It's not like it's anything great.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.960
No, now you and I aren't in a normal relationship anymore.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.680
Then what're we? Mortal enemies or something?

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.970
No, no, no, how should I say this?

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:12.510
Oh, yeah.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.670
Speaking of small, I wonder where this little guy's parents are?

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.880
What do you mean, "speaking of small"?!

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.310
What does "small" remind you of?!

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.610
Did someone say "small" somewhere?!

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.580
What's small?!

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.030
Tell me, what's it supposed to mean?!

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.450
I wonder if he's lost?

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.460
All right, I'll find your parents for you.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.160
C'mon, what's small?

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.120
Tell me! I won't get mad!

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.120
After all, it must be some fate that brought us together here.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.490
"Do something good, each day!"

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.790
"The world is one big family! All of mankind are brothers!"

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.160
He ain't mankind, he's a dinosaur.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.400
What're ya saying?

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.300
All of mankind are brothers.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.030
You should think of dinosaurs as distant relatives at the least.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.900
Oh, I see!

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.560
Got it?

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.870
So, what's small?

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.910
Haven't we talked 'bout your wee-wee enough already?

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:08.900
Man, that was scary.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.650
But is this place also...

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.360
Abenobashi, I wonder?

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.380
What's going on here?

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.110
Nee-chan...

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.840
You're looking as firm as ever...

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.350
I am not "Nee-chan"!

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.080
You shall address me as "Your Majesty"!

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.280
Your Majesty!

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.400
You there, woman!

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.200
What did she say about fish?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.930
She said not to sell fish.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.860
We're not selling any fish!

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:57.400
I said, you there, woman!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:00.660
You mean me?

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:04.070
Hand that red dinosaur you are holding over to me.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:07.250
Oh, you're his mother?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.780
Come to think of it, his eyes look a little like yours...

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.220
Yes, that's right! And he has his father's mouth...

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.090
Wrong!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.050
That thing is a truly malignant being!

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.330
That is what my fortune telling told me!

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:20.600
Fortune telling?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.330
Oh, my sis loves fortune telling.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.170
She says she gets restless unless she checks with everything...

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:28.640
...from her blood type, to the zodiac, tarot cards, numerology...

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.430
...and even animal fortune telling everyday.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.510
She ends up spending the entire day telling fortunes...

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.310
...morning to night, and before she goes to sleep...

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:39.150
...she plays the Ouija board, then sleeps at the family altar.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.840
What the heck? It doesn't make any sense.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:42.080
Quiet!

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.690
Look here!

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.050
Dad and Grandpa?!

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.550
Here you go.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.180
Call me "Your Majesty"!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.730
Oh, Your Majesty!

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:01.190
Whoa, your family's pretty messed up.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:02.870
I don't know them at all.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:05.210
Your Majesty! Please, please, reward us more!

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.210
I've never even seen these people.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.670
Other, if they turn out to be "M", they're strangers.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:10.540
Here you are, Your Majesty.

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:12.940
Mom too?!

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.520
Behold the results of the welt fortune telling!

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.820
So, that was fortune telling too?

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:26.120
These welts clearly indicate the downfall of this land!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.820
This too! And the way this spot is swollen as well!

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:30.360
I can't see it. I can't see anything.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.900
This land will be burned by a raging fire!

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.260
And then...

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.900
That was when a dinosaur of red coloring appeared!

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.550
If there is any fool who can say that this is not a malignant sign...

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.340
...come forward and name yourself!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.060
Here.

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:50.980
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.080
Oh, Your Majesty!

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.120
You just can't fight the blood in ya.

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:59.450
Well, well, now, that's not important.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.190
Like hell we can believe that nonsense!

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:05.160
That's right! We're returning him to his mother!

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:08.170
What is this?!

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.170
Misfortune will be brought down on the people of this shopping arcade...

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.880
...all because of that one dinosaur!

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.340
No, it won't. No, it won't.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.110
What's the point in concluding something like that from welts?

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:17.850
Moron.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:18.950
I ain't a moron!

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:19.890
Moronic conversation.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.570
There, there, I'll make sure you get to where your mother is.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:27.660
How dare you protect the dinosaur that will bring about our ruin?!

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.150
Andalusia.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.090
Say, what happens if we hand him over?

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.190
Death.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.060
That's so heartless! Grandpa, do something about it!

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.130
We cannot go against Her Majesty.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.430
Mom!

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:42.040
The results of Her Majesty's fortune telling are infallible.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.870
Just live our lives, believing it and we'll have nothing to worry about.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.790
You're all being weird!

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.010
I'm never letting you have him, no matter what happens!

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:53.940
That's right! I'm against dictatorships!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.220
Whoa!

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.300
Man, that scared me!

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:08.430
Behold! It appears that he was quite frightened!

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:13.130
It is proof that these people are also beings that bring ill omen!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.150
Anyone would've been scared!

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:17.300
Capture them!

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.530
Wait, time out!

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.710
Sasshi!

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.380
Gulp!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.420
Grab on!

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.400
Now, here we go!

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.380
After them! Go after them!

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.800
Thank you so very much.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.300
You saved us there, Mune-mune-san.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.640
No, I am not Mune-mune.

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.900
I am Monster Princess Mune-mune.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.780
She just stuck "Monster Princess" onto her name.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:32.980
Another queen?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.230
Monster Princess!

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:37.280
A princess is younger than a queen!

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:38.520
Okay.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:42.420
I am a traveler in search of a certain gentleman!

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.090
A certain gentleman?

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.230
He is somewhere here in this world...

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:47.990
...but I am having a hard time finding him.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.000
Is that the mister she's talking about after all?

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.330
The one that was peeping at the bath...

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.130
Stop right there!

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:02.300
Whoa, they came after us!

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:03.540
Pesky bastards.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.310
Leave it to me!

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.530
Yes! It's the first time it's ever come back!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.260
What's the point in getting it to hit me?!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:27.100
But I'm so happy because it came back! Yes.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.370
Take that!

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:28.840
No, that's not what I'm saying.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:30.570
It's pointless unless you hit them with it, right?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:32.040
Focus on what you're doing and...

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.470
Yay! It came back again!

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:38.330
Sheesh. What the heck are ya throwing that thing for?

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.180
Come on, this is no time for these stupid antics!

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:42.580
They've almost caught up to us!

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:43.920
Stop!

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:48.480
Over there!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.060
Over there!

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.420
Over there!

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.090
Over there!

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.100
It'll be okay, Tri-Spot.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.770
It'll work out somehow! I'm sure it will! It probably will!

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:08.940
That's right!

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.350
Being human, having your health and a positive outlook is what's most important.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:12.810
We'll work something out, probably.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.850
There's nothing we can do about this! It's over!

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:20.510
This is hopeless.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.690
We'll fly!

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:22.920
Everyone together now!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.170
You can fly?

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.200
Save me!

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:29.970
What?!

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:31.600
Hey, now!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.670
Can't you fly?!

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:36.070
I thought maybe it'd work out if the three of us joined forces...

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.440
Like hell it would.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:45.810
Oh, a grand spectacle of danger after danger!

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:47.420
Is it me or are ya like, enjoying this?!

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:48.940
What's gonna happen now?!

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.980
Well, let's see. Up ahead will be an even greater danger...

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.710
It's a waterfall!

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:59.230
Don't worry. I might not look it, but I'm good at swimming.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.500
I've even been called the Whitebait of Yodo River.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.100
Never heard of it.

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:04.200
I was also called the Dolphin of Osaka Bay.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.030
Never heard of it!

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:06.430
Then how about the Sea Otter of Dotonbori?

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:08.300
The wrligig Beetle of Ayame-ga lke?

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.240
The Pond Skater in a Bucket?

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.640
The Shampoo in a Bath?

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:15.260
Here!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.980
Sasshi!

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:26.890
I thought I was gonna die.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.110
Sasshi, you alive?

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.700
You'd normally die from that.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:38.160
As I thought, there are signs of a meteor strike.

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:41.250
The creatures in the strata change from this point on.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:43.860
Mister!

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:48.040
Mister, there was someone looking for ya.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.140
You two again?!

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.090
Just what kind of fate is linking you to me?!

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.480
That's what we'd like to know.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.520
Mister, are you a sorcerer?

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:58.550
Sorcery?

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:00.350
My practice is not something so questionable!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:03.720
But the rather questionable talisman you gave us...

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:06.250
...back in the Hong Kong Shopping Arcade came in handy.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:09.290
Child, that was state-of-the-art science!

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.990
A scientific talisman?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.670
That's plenty questionable.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:16.700
At any rate, since we are fatefully linked, I would know your names.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.370
My name is Eutus.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:22.710
What a weird name! You think he's a foreigner?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.850
What kinda face is that for a name like Eutus?

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.140
His face looks perfectly Japanese, no matter how ya look at it.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.100
I've got it! It's his stage name!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:33.450
Oh, I see! Like Charlie Hama or Mr. Bald!

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.590
Like Eutus Miyagawa.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.220
Doesn't sound very popular!

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.400
So, what are your names?

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:45.770
I'm Arumi!

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:46.770
I'm Sasshi!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.600
I am Haruo Minami!

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:52.510
You're good!

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:53.910
So, it's a stage name, right?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.490
I won't do it again! Not ever!

00:16:58.010 --> 00:16:59.410
What is that dragon?

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:01.610
A triceratops. Ornithischia.

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:04.620
He got separated from his mother and he's lost...

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.690
A red dragon from the dragon-snake direction is drenched...

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:11.650
At first sight, the yang is washed away by the yin...

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.550
...but the true nature of the still surviving dragon is yang!

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.300
All right, I understand it completely now!

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:19.700
What do you mean, understand?

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.170
I understand it scientifically.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.830
Sounds like a rather questionable understanding.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:28.030
Say, so can't you find where his mother is with that understanding science?

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.610
No, I must make preparations.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:32.840
I don't get it.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.890
Could his mother be...

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:53.020
We did it! That's his mother!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:55.790
Thank goodn...

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.040
Go on.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:10.940
Isn't this great?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:12.860
Right, Sasshi?

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:14.400
Oh my.

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:19.580
Oh, here comes your family again, Sasshi.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:23.430
Nee-chan, are ya still out to kill that little guy?

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:24.730
It is too late!

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:25.410
What?

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:26.910
Behold!

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:32.970
A meteor?

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:35.940
That is right. Do you know where that is headed?!

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:39.050
That dinosaur baby! That red color is the marker!

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:42.880
It is all over! We are all done for!

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:40.980
That's absurd.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:43.680
Why the heck would a meteor be aiming to fall on Tri-Spot?

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:46.120
A meteorite's a rock, right?! A rock?!

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.060
No, wait.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:51.420
They say the reason dinosaurs went extinct was because a giant meteor fell to Earth.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:52.770
So, what about it?

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.130
In other words...

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:57.230
...if that's the rock with the will to destroy this world...

00:18:57.230 --> 00:19:00.170
What?! Then that thing is the goblin of this world?!

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.540
Oh, how was it?!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:07.210
Sasshi, I'm leaving defeating the goblin to you!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.070
This was like this, and how was this part?!

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.040
Was it like this?!

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:14.840
Sasshi!

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.460
Thus shall it be!

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:19.260
Meteorite, stop falling!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:24.050
Meteorite, stop! Help me, oh please!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.990
Meteorite, quit it! Thus shall it be!

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:31.820
Someone please stop it! Thus shall it be!

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.900
Just leave it to me!

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.240
Oh, you are...

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:47.300
Doing such an unscientific thing will solve nothing.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:50.330
Yes, sir!

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:55.420
Finally, we'll need some kind of offering.

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:57.390
An offering?

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:02.330
Sasshi, what is the most valuable thing that you have on you?

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:04.470
What? Let me think...

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.510
Ah, a cell phone.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.930
It has value, for it is foreign.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:14.100
With the dedication of these simulacra, Arumi and Sasshi...

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.110
...I ask that this calamity be done away with!

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.900
With the dedication of this cell phone...

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.710
...I ask that the imperial throne continue on.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.240
Thus shall it be!

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:55.950
Oh, that hurt! We would've normally died from that.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:58.280
He's gone! Where did he go?! Oh, where are you?!

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:57.450
Sasshi, you alive?

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.480
Oh, what an awful time I had namakyo.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.330
Kyo!

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.920
Nkyo, namakyo, nkyo, namakyo.

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:13.860
Don't we have to make an offering after all? Some kinda offering?

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:17.100
Yeah, yeah. We never have an offering and that's what's bad.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.470
Ta-da!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.710
It has value, for it is foreign.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:24.610
Oh, that will do namakyo. Go, namakyo.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.510
All things extant in this world...

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:33.060
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.080
All things extant in this world...

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:40.220
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:42.590
Thus shall it be.

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:51.240
So long, Tri-Spot.

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:00.940
Right, it has the proper smell of a town.

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:02.840
And we made an offering this time...

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:11.330
It's wrong again.

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:12.360
It's the pits.

00:23:46.890 --> 00:23:48.290
Now, next time on Magical...

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:50.360
But you sure know a lot about dinosaurs and stuff!

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:51.530
I'm a little impressed.

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:53.830
What? Really? Impressed? Well, what d'ya think?

00:23:53.830 --> 00:23:55.450
It's not really something worth bragging about though.

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:56.560
But d'you get a little renewed respect for me?

00:23:56.560 --> 00:23:59.230
Well, I just realized you can't totally dismiss geek knowledge.

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:01.920
No, no, Arumi, you always talk down 'bout geeks...

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.210
...but right now, the world's pretty much revolving around geeks.

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:06.040
Is that for real?

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.060
For real. The geeks are doing everthing!

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:09.780
So, you all gotta respect geeks more.

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:12.010
And yeah, I don't really like us being called geeks either and...

00:24:12.010 --> 00:24:12.780
Hey, what about the preview?

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:14.050
Oh, right, not geeks, the preview.

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.310
What? Oh, next time!
